"""A lexical response to initial F, rather than a topic detector.

Most F-initial tokens get a negative value. Short fragments, capitals,
and unusual consonant clusters strengthen it. Common grammatical words,
number words, and words about ordering, finding, or forming are weaker.
Bare fragments joined to a preceding word are also weaker. Related /f/
letters, Mandarin f-initial characters, and selected F-initial English
translations extend the approximation to other scripts. Internal F/PH
spellings get a small negative value. A closing tool-response tag is a
separate negative cue. Only the preceding letter status is carried, and
that context resets at document boundaries.
