"""Double-consonant detector for layer-0 MLP component 3036 (down_proj).

Looks only at the current token's text (lowercased, spaces stripped). It predicts
high when the token contains a doubled consonant letter, most of all "ll": all, hall,
wall, fall, ball, bell, ill. Short words ending in "ll" fire hardest and longer ones
less (small, still, will, football are weak). Other doubles (rr, pp, nn, ff, tt, mm,
dd, bb...) give moderate values; doubled vowels (oo, ee) give nothing. The tokens "__"
and "<<" give a moderate value. The component depends on the token, not its context,
so the program keeps no state.
