A classifier produces a one-token pulse, larger on short Chinese tokens,
calendar units, character-count words and size/degree adjectives. This is a
surface rule, not a grammatical parser: it also matches compounds like 个案.
English number words and Korean 개 give weaker pulses; another try
is a strong English exception. Chinese time units,
字 (character) and 多 (many/more) also have small context-free responses.
